  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nIntrepid is a self-hostable, open-source URL shortener designed to provide users with the ability to brand their URLs and maintain control over their data. Based on the platform Polr, the application aims to offer a quick and modern approach to link shortening with a robust API.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to develop an efficient, self-hosted URL shortening solution that allows users to manage and brand their own links while providing data control and insights into link usage.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Primary Users: Individuals and organizations seeking a customizable and private link shortening service.\n- Administrators: Responsible for maintaining the application, managing user accounts, and overseeing system functionalities.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- User Registration & Management: \n  - Users can register and manage their accounts, including setting up passwords and recovery keys.\n  - Specific user roles and permissions are assigned for accessing various functionalities.\n\n- Link Creation & Management:\n  - Users can create shortened URLs from long URLs, with options for branding and customization.\n  - Option to generate custom URLs and API-based links.\n\n- Tracking & Analytics:\n  - The system logs clicks, including IP addresses, countries, referers, and user agents.\n  - Provides click analytics for each link, such as total clicks and click sources.\n\n- API Functionality:\n  - A robust API allows programmatic access to shortening features, including link creation and management.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: \n  - The application should perform efficiently under varying loads, supporting both individual and organizational use.\n\n- Security:\n  - Ensure secure processing of user data and protection against unauthorized API usage through keys and quotas.\n\n- Scalability:\n  - The system should support scaling to accommodate increasing numbers of users and links, while maintaining performance.\n\n- Availability:\n  - The application should be reliably available for use, with minimal downtime and timely updates to address user needs and security patches.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0074\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `recovery_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'user',\n  `api_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `api_quota` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_username_unique` (`username`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_email_unique` (`email`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_api_key_unique` (`api_key`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `links` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `long_url` text NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_custom` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `is_api_created` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `click_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `links_slug_unique` (`slug`),\n  KEY `links_user_id_index` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `links_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `clicks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `link_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `referer` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_agent` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `clicked_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `clicks_link_id_index` (`link_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `clicks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`link_id`) REFERENCES `links` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
